<title>CHINA: China to hike sugar output to 10 mln T by 2000.</title>
<headline>China to hike sugar output to 10 mln T by 2000.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>China aims to boost annual sugar production to 10 million tonnes by the year 2000 and to 13 million tonnes by the year 2010, the Market Daily newspaper said on Monday.</p>
<p>Average per capita consumption is expected to increase to 8.7 kg in 2000 and to 9.5 kg by the year 2010 from the current 6.0 kg, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>China aims to produce 6.53 million tonnes of sugar in 1996, up from 5.65 million tonnes in 1995, and spurred by an increase in the state purchasing price, officials have said.</p>
</text>
